Package: sharedstat
Title: Diagnose and Correct Statistics Built from a Shared Component
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Rui", "Chen", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "Rui.Chen@campus.lmu.de")
Author: Rui Chen [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Rui Chen <Rui.Chen@campus.lmu.de>
Description: Comparative designs routinely form a statistic from a difference, a ratio or a
    residual of two quantities that share a component: a divergence measured against a shared
    reference arm, a 'trans' term obtained by subtracting a 'cis' term, a count of significant
    genes read as an ordering of effect sizes, or an interaction contrast on compositional counts.
    Each construction has an algebraic failure mode that is older than genomics. This package
    implements the five admission checks, the two estimators and the attenuation result described
    in the accompanying paper, together with a known-truth simulator in which compositionality
    emerges from closed-sum sampling rather than being imposed. It ranks no method as more accurate
    than another and describes no standard method as biased; what it provides is the size of each
    artefact relative to the effect being estimated, and the procedure that follows.
